Windows: avoid doubled separators in directory enumeration

OpenDirectory receives a directory path with a trailing separator. Reversed
suffix selection appends a second separator, tolerated by ordinary Win32
paths but rejected for extended-length paths. Select the suffix according
to the separator already present. Keep the requested profile location.

--- a/sal/osl/w32/file_dirvol.cxx
+++ b/sal/osl/w32/file_dirvol.cxx
@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@
         return nullptr;
 
     std::u16string_view suffix;
-    if (!path.endsWith(u"\\"))
+    if (path.endsWith(u"\\"))
         suffix = u"*.*";
     else
         suffix = u"\\*.*";
